        <name>links_</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::utils::double_list::links_</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The list top node used to point to <bold>head</bold> and <bold>tail</bold> nodes. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This member stores the internal links node for the list. The <bold>next</bold> pointer of this node points to the head of the list, and the <bold>previous</bold> pointer points to the tail. For an empty list, both pointers refer to the node itself, simplifying list management and boundary checks. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
